## 2. Component graph and data flow

Static instrument. No runtime services; every node is an act performed by the executing worker.

```
   spec/SAEOS-1 §4.3            spec/SAEOS-1 §9/A8
   (node types + fields)        (claim under test)
            │                            │
            ▼                            │
   ┌──────────────────┐                  │
   │ C1 SchemaLoader  │                  │
   │ → FieldMatrix F  │                  │
   └────────┬─────────┘                  │
            │                            │
 ledger/ ───┼──► ┌──────────────────┐    │
 reviews/   │    │ C2 GoalSelector  │    │
 tasks/ ────┘    │ → G = {g1,g2,g3} │    │
                 └────────┬─────────┘    │
                          │              │
                          ▼              │
                 ┌──────────────────┐    │
                 │ C3 Extractor     │    │  hand-extraction, per (goal × node × field)
                 │ → Verdict cells  │    │
                 └────────┬─────────┘    │
                          ▼              │
                 ┌──────────────────┐    │
                 │ C4 Scorer        │    │
                 │ → fidelity,      │    │
                 │   loss_ratio,    │    │
                 │   veto set       │    │
                 └────────┬─────────┘    │
                          ▼              ▼
                 ┌─────────────────────────────┐
                 │ C5 VerdictGate              │
                 │ pre-registered rule (§3.4)  │
                 │ → GO | NO-GO                │
                 └────────┬────────────────────┘
                          ▼
        reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md
```

### Interfaces

| Component | Input | Output | Contract |
|---|---|---|---|
| **C1** SchemaLoader | §4.3 text | `F = [(node_type, field)]` | Every field in §4.3 appears exactly once. `|F|` is the per-goal denominator. No invented fields; no dropped fields. |
| **C2** GoalSelector | `ledger/`, `reviews/tasks/` | `G`, `|G| = 3` | Selection rule §3.4 applied and *recorded* before extraction begins. |
| **C3** Extractor | `g ∈ G`, `F` | verdict ∈ {extractable, partial, absent} per cell, + evidence span | Every cell carries a pointer into the source goal or the literal `—` for `absent`. No cell left blank. |
| **C4** Scorer | verdict cells | `fidelity`, `loss_ratio`, `veto_fields` | Pure function of §3.1–3.3. No judgement. |
| **C5** VerdictGate | scorer output | `GO` \| `NO-GO` | Pure function of §3.4. **Rule is fixed before C3 runs.** |

**Directionality is the integrity property.** C5 must not be able to reach back and revise C2's sample
or C3's cells. If the verdict is disliked, the correct move is to record it and open a follow-up — not
to re-select goals. Re-running C2 after seeing a C5 output invalidates the probe and must be disclosed
in the output as `sample_reselected: true`.

