| Founder/orchestrator — what unblocks this? | yes | §0 remediation, §0 B4 |

**Orphans / gaps — stated, not hidden:**

- **G1** The §4.3 node types are *not enumerated here.* `spec/` is absent and I will not invent a
  schema. `F` is a hole C1 fills at execution time. Everything downstream is parameterized over `|F|`,
  so no rework is implied — but this document does not and cannot tell you what the node types are.
- **G2** The 0.30 threshold is a judgement, not a derivation. It is pre-registered so it cannot be
  moved post-hoc, but it is not itself evidence-backed. A reviewer may substitute a different value —
  **before** execution, in writing.
- **G3** Single-rater extraction (A5). No inter-rater agreement statistic. For a spike this is
  acceptable; if the result is used to justify building SAKG, a second rater on ≥1 goal is warranted.
- **G4** n=3 is fixed by the objective. It supports a NO-GO (one structural absence is a real finding)
  far better than a GO (3 clean goals is weak evidence the schema generalizes). **An asymmetry the
  reader of the eventual GO must hold onto.**

